{"context":"Steward mixes deterministic orchestration with LLM workers. Without a stated boundary, control-flow decisions could drift into prompts, making runs unreproducible and hard to audit.","decision":"CODE decides which/when/if (scheduling, selection, gating, retries, sizing) and the LLM decides what (content) only inside ACP worker sessions. No LLM output may drive control flow. All control-flow decision points are code-owned and enumerated.","consequences":"Runs are reproducible given identical inputs; failures are debuggable without reading model output. Content quality depends on the worker, not the loop. Cost: content-inflected decisions must be modeled explicitly in code/policy.","alternativesConsidered":"LLM-decided scheduling (rejected: non-deterministic, unauditable). Fully code-driven content (rejected: no agent value). A hybrid where the LLM may veto a step (rejected: control-flow leakage).","appliesTo":["eka-steward/**"]}